Z||000000||Earne||03-27-2000||08:28 AM||||Anyone have the  rubber weather strip for the front edge of the deck lid, in really good condition, and willing to part with it?  I need one for an '86.5 GT with the clips that hold it on.<P>This is the rubber piece that Pontiac took off as part of one of the recalls.  It's on the deck lid just beneath the rear window.  I'm not convinced that it is a hazard, prevents a ton of water going directly on the front manifold and plugs, and really looks like something is missing without one.<P>Anyone have any opinion of the "hazards" of reinstalling this piece?  I understand it was removed to reduce heat retention.<P>I have another gray, leather, cobrahead shaped autoshift knob or an excellent 5 ch eqlzr cass stereo from my '86, to trade or will buy outright.  Guys, for the radio, the weather seal should look like new.<P>Earne (ToyMaker)||||reg||5
